EFS configuration 
1)	Create iamserviceaccount
eksctl create iamserviceaccount   --name efs-csi-controller-sa   --namespace kube-system   --cluster $cluster_name   --role-name $role_name   --attach-policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy   --approve
2)	TRUST_POLICY and Create addon
TRUST_POLICY=$(aws iam get-role --output json --role-name $role_name --query 'Role.AssumeRolePolicyDocument' | \
    sed -e 's/efs-csi-controller-sa/efs-csi-*/' -e 's/StringEquals/StringLike/')

aws iam update-assume-role-policy --role-name $role_name --policy-document "$TRUST_POLICY"

export SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ROLE_ARN=arn:aws:iam::157298730309:role/AmazonEKS_EFS_CSI_DriverRole
eksctl create addon   --name aws-efs-csi-driver   --cluster $cluster_name   --region ap-south-1   --service-account-role-arn ${SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ROLE_ARN}   --force

Create custom storage class 
efs-sc.yaml
-----------------------------
apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: efs-sc
  annotations:
    storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class: "true"
provisioner: efs.csi.aws.com
parameters:
  provisioningMode: efs-ap
  fileSystemId: fs-02945ccfd93dae06a
  directoryPerms: "700"
reclaimPolicy: Retain
volumeBindingMode: Immediate
allowVolumeExpansion: true
kubectl apply -f  efs-sc.yaml

NOTE:
  1)security group of  EFS must be add EFS port 2049 of EKS security group
  2) A Kubernetes service account configured with IRSA (IAM Role for Service Account), using the AWS-managed policy AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy, with permissions to create the aws-efs-csi-driver add-on
3) One EFS file system created in the same VPC as the EKS cluster:
 4)   Security group inbound rule allowing traffic on port 2049 from the EKS cluster security group.
5)	Dynamic access point creation in EFS should be allowed from EKS.
S3 ACCESS
1)	S3 bucket connectivity should be enabled for the EKS cluster
RDS CONNECTIVITY 
1)	An RDS PostgreSQL database configured to allow connectivity from the EKS cluster:
2)	The RDS security group should permit access from the EKS cluster security group.
3)	The RDS instance should reside in the same VPC as the EKS cluster.


